# The C library, such as it is, and the startup stub.
#
# Nothing is built here. Both system/ and apps/ compile crt0.s and
# ulib.c into every program directly, because there are no archives and
# no linker script magic to make a .a worth having -- five files and a
# dozen programs do not need a library format between them.
#
# What this directory IS for is saying that those files belong to
# neither of the two sets of programs and are shared by both.
